WEBVTT

00:00:00.281 --> 00:00:01.546
Here's a list of numbers:

00:00:02.209 --> 00:00:02.771
minus one,

00:00:03.273 --> 00:00:03.655
zero,

00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:05.402
nine, thirty-two.

00:00:06.265 --> 00:00:08.894
They're the positions of a moving particle, read

00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:10.058
at one, two,

00:00:10.561 --> 00:00:11.905
three and four seconds.

00:00:12.989 --> 00:00:14.873
A list of numbers in a fixed order,

00:00:15.034 --> 00:00:16.718
like this, is called a sequence.

00:00:17.522 --> 00:00:18.908
Sequences are everywhere.

00:00:19.592 --> 00:00:21.679
At a cricket match, read the scoreboard at

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.722
the end of each over.

00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:25.393
The runs scored in each over make one

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.526
sequence, and those end-of-over totals make another.

00:00:29.309 --> 00:00:31.835
So what exactly is a sequence, and how

00:00:31.856 --> 00:00:33.459
do we add up its terms neatly?

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:36.701
A sequence is an ordered list of objects,

00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:37.644
usually numbers.

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:40.533
Each object is called a term, and every

00:00:40.594 --> 00:00:43.744
term has a position: first, second, third, and

00:00:43.786 --> 00:00:44.086
so on.

00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:47.197
We write a sub n for the term

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:49.607
in position n, where n is a positive

00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:50.129
whole number.

00:00:50.912 --> 00:00:53.717
Say one team scores one, three, five and

00:00:53.858 --> 00:00:55.741
seven runs in the first four overs.

00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:58.321
Here, a sub three is five.

00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:00.813
The three is the position, the third over,

00:01:01.155 --> 00:01:03.182
and the five is the value, the runs.

00:01:03.926 --> 00:01:05.890
Now a second team scores the same runs

00:01:06.051 --> 00:01:08.436
in reverse: seven, five, three, one.

00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:11.146
After four overs, both teams have sixteen.

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:12.814
But after the first over,

00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:15.486
one scoreboard shows one, and the other shows

00:01:15.568 --> 00:01:15.848
seven.

00:01:16.692 --> 00:01:19.220
The positions stay put and the values move.

00:01:19.742 --> 00:01:21.969
That's why order matters, and why these are

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:22.852
different sequences.

00:01:23.636 --> 00:01:25.728
Often a rule gives each term from its

00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:26.150
position.

00:01:26.956 --> 00:01:29.529
Say a team scores two n runs in

00:01:29.731 --> 00:01:30.313
over n.

00:01:31.098 --> 00:01:33.891
Put in n equals one, and a sub

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:34.655
one is two.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.847
Then come four, six, eight and ten.

00:01:38.551 --> 00:01:40.078
The rule only needs the position.

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:43.228
So to find a sub fifty, put in

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.097
fifty and get one hundred, without listing the

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:47.521
first forty-nine terms.

00:01:48.465 --> 00:01:50.708
If the game stops after five overs, the

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:53.733
list stops at ten, its fifth term, so

00:01:53.814 --> 00:01:55.076
it's a finite sequence.

00:01:55.839 --> 00:01:58.550
A finite sequence ends at some last term,

00:01:59.093 --> 00:01:59.956
a sub m.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:00.722
Here m

00:02:01.309 --> 00:02:01.772
is five.

00:02:02.581 --> 00:02:05.448
But if the list never stops, two, four,

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.955
six, eight, ten, and so on forever,

00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:09.721
it's an infinite sequence.

00:02:10.364 --> 00:02:12.031
We show that with three dots at the

00:02:12.092 --> 00:02:12.231
end.

00:02:12.862 --> 00:02:14.672
Now add the runs up as we go,

00:02:15.316 --> 00:02:16.181
like the scoreboard does.

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:18.406
After one over, the total is S

00:02:18.907 --> 00:02:20.330
one, just the first term,

00:02:20.952 --> 00:02:21.132
two.

00:02:22.135 --> 00:02:24.285
S two adds the first two terms: two

00:02:24.366 --> 00:02:25.893
plus four is six.

00:02:26.557 --> 00:02:29.636
Then the scoreboard shows twelve, twenty and thirty.

00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:30.982
In general,

00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:33.332
S sub n is the sum of the

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:34.578
first n terms.

00:02:35.302 --> 00:02:37.955
It's called the nth partial sum, a running

00:02:37.996 --> 00:02:38.297
total.

00:02:39.363 --> 00:02:42.829
Notice that the totals, two, six, twelve, twenty,

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:43.470
thirty,

00:02:43.992 --> 00:02:45.594
make a new sequence of their own.

00:02:46.256 --> 00:02:47.820
And each total is the one before it,

00:02:48.162 --> 00:02:49.404
plus one more over.

00:02:50.207 --> 00:02:53.752
So S five minus S four leaves just

00:02:53.793 --> 00:02:54.894
the fifth over's runs:

00:02:55.556 --> 00:02:57.358
thirty minus twenty is ten.

00:02:58.041 --> 00:03:00.447
What if the sequence is infinite, like a

00:03:00.487 --> 00:03:02.051
game whose overs never end?

00:03:02.793 --> 00:03:04.857
Then the sum of all its terms, a

00:03:04.897 --> 00:03:06.921
sub one plus a sub two plus a

00:03:06.941 --> 00:03:09.306
sub three, and so on, is called a

00:03:09.426 --> 00:03:09.847
series.

00:03:10.611 --> 00:03:12.223
The partial sums are the steps on the

00:03:12.263 --> 00:03:12.445
way.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.918
For two, plus four, plus six, and so

00:03:15.999 --> 00:03:18.507
on, the scoreboard just keeps climbing, so this

00:03:18.527 --> 00:03:19.711
series has no total.

00:03:20.595 --> 00:03:22.580
Some series do settle on a number, and

00:03:22.621 --> 00:03:24.305
we'll see which ones in a later video.

00:03:25.068 --> 00:03:25.228
So,

00:03:25.811 --> 00:03:28.218
S sub n means the first n terms.

00:03:28.763 --> 00:03:30.177
A series means all of them.

00:03:30.821 --> 00:03:32.830
Writing long sums out is slow,

00:03:33.332 --> 00:03:35.039
so we use sigma notation.

00:03:35.903 --> 00:03:37.229
Take the first team's runs again:

00:03:37.912 --> 00:03:40.161
one, three, five, seven.

00:03:41.045 --> 00:03:43.495
This big symbol is the Greek capital letter

00:03:43.716 --> 00:03:45.744
sigma, and it means add.

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:47.170
Underneath,

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.906
k equals one tells you where to start.

00:03:50.671 --> 00:03:52.885
On top, four tells you where to stop.

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:56.122
And two k minus one, on the right,

00:03:56.566 --> 00:03:57.791
is the rule for each term.

00:03:58.536 --> 00:04:00.530
Each value of k makes one term.

00:04:01.356 --> 00:04:02.657
Put in k equals one,

00:04:03.279 --> 00:04:03.518
two,

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.343
three and four, to get one,

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:07.145
three,

00:04:07.687 --> 00:04:08.788
five and seven.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.573
Add them up, and the sum is sixteen,

00:04:12.216 --> 00:04:13.738
Team A's score after four overs.

00:04:14.348 --> 00:04:16.196
The start doesn't have to be one.

00:04:16.919 --> 00:04:19.064
Here's the sum from k equals three to

00:04:19.145 --> 00:04:20.507
seven, of k squared.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.384
The first term uses k equals three, so

00:04:23.426 --> 00:04:23.868
it's nine.

00:04:24.412 --> 00:04:27.650
Then come sixteen, twenty-five, thirty-six and forty-nine.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:31.305
That's five terms, not seven, because seven minus

00:04:31.346 --> 00:04:33.253
three is four, plus one for the first

00:04:33.294 --> 00:04:33.454
term.

00:04:34.198 --> 00:04:36.065
The total is one hundred and thirty-five.

00:04:36.969 --> 00:04:39.432
In general, the sum from k equals i

00:04:39.493 --> 00:04:41.635
to j, of a sub k,

00:04:42.237 --> 00:04:45.000
adds every term from a sub i up

00:04:45.042 --> 00:04:45.742
to a sub j.

00:04:46.724 --> 00:04:48.371
And k is just a counter.

00:04:49.296 --> 00:04:51.683
Use m instead, and the sum is exactly

00:04:51.745 --> 00:04:52.045
the same.

00:04:52.608 --> 00:04:53.373
Let's go the other way.

00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:56.629
A sequence has a sub n equals n

00:04:56.691 --> 00:04:58.538
squared minus n plus one.

00:04:59.061 --> 00:05:02.008
Its first five terms are one, three, seven,

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.612
thirteen and twenty-one.

00:05:04.094 --> 00:05:06.503
Their sum, S five, is forty-five.

00:05:07.126 --> 00:05:09.947
To write S five in sigma notation, swap

00:05:10.188 --> 00:05:12.329
n for the counter k, start at one

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.430
and stop at five.

00:05:13.911 --> 00:05:15.958
So S five is the sum, from k

00:05:15.999 --> 00:05:18.909
equals one to five, of k squared minus

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:19.873
k plus one.

00:05:20.336 --> 00:05:22.484
That's forty-five again, written in one line.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.165
Now write a sum from words.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.039
Write the sum of the first ten odd

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.727
numbers in sigma notation.

00:05:30.492 --> 00:05:32.729
First, find a rule for the odd numbers.

00:05:33.613 --> 00:05:35.495
One, three, five, seven:

00:05:36.297 --> 00:05:38.579
each one is one less than an even

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:38.879
number,

00:05:39.421 --> 00:05:41.984
so the kth odd number is two k

00:05:42.045 --> 00:05:42.565
minus one.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.525
Check: k equals one gives one.

00:05:46.534 --> 00:05:48.046
Next, the start and the stop.

00:05:48.731 --> 00:05:51.322
The first ten odd numbers means k goes

00:05:51.363 --> 00:05:52.507
from one to ten.

00:05:53.271 --> 00:05:55.721
So it's the sum, from k equals one

00:05:55.843 --> 00:05:58.011
to ten, of two k minus one.

00:05:58.876 --> 00:06:01.086
The last term is two times ten, minus

00:06:01.228 --> 00:06:02.352
one, which is nineteen.

00:06:03.056 --> 00:06:04.964
And all ten add to one hundred.

00:06:05.637 --> 00:06:07.153
Here's a way to read any sigma.

00:06:07.722 --> 00:06:08.694
Bottom: start.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.068
Top: stop.

00:06:10.753 --> 00:06:12.559
And the number of terms is the top

00:06:12.781 --> 00:06:14.306
minus the bottom, plus one.

00:06:14.949 --> 00:06:17.432
From five to nine, that's five terms, not

00:06:17.493 --> 00:06:17.692
four.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:20.827
Your turn.

00:06:21.557 --> 00:06:24.347
Evaluate the sum, from k equals two to

00:06:24.428 --> 00:06:26.877
five, of four k minus three.

00:06:27.803 --> 00:06:28.890
Pause here to answer.

00:06:39.648 --> 00:06:41.171
Start at k equals two:

00:06:41.874 --> 00:06:44.020
four times two, minus three, is five.

00:06:44.683 --> 00:06:47.333
Then come nine, thirteen and seventeen.

00:06:47.896 --> 00:06:50.595
That's four terms, and they add to forty-four.

00:06:51.482 --> 00:06:52.468
Twenty-eight is wrong.

00:06:53.073 --> 00:06:55.682
It starts at k equals one, and stops

00:06:55.863 --> 00:06:56.565
one term early.

00:06:58.197 --> 00:06:58.642
Last one.

00:06:59.187 --> 00:07:01.976
A sequence has a sub n equals ten

00:07:02.117 --> 00:07:02.799
minus two n.

00:07:03.683 --> 00:07:06.514
Find S four, and write S four in

00:07:06.656 --> 00:07:07.518
sigma notation.

00:07:08.183 --> 00:07:09.009
Pause here to answer.

00:07:19.855 --> 00:07:22.623
The first four terms are eight, six, four

00:07:22.725 --> 00:07:23.105
and two.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.103
S four adds all four of them, to

00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:26.586
make twenty.

00:07:27.452 --> 00:07:30.338
In sigma notation, it's the sum, from k

00:07:30.479 --> 00:07:33.305
equals one to four, of ten minus two

00:07:33.366 --> 00:07:33.526
k.

00:07:34.431 --> 00:07:35.217
Two is wrong.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.427
That's a sub four, the fourth term, not

00:07:38.468 --> 00:07:39.972
the sum of the first four terms.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.722
So a sequence is an ordered list,

00:07:44.342 --> 00:07:46.184
a sub n is the term in position

00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:46.524
n,

00:07:47.285 --> 00:07:49.106
S sub n adds up the first n

00:07:49.186 --> 00:07:52.129
terms, and sigma writes a sum in one

00:07:52.189 --> 00:07:52.469
line.

00:07:53.071 --> 00:07:54.599
Now look at a stack of chairs.

00:07:55.242 --> 00:07:57.110
One chair is eighty centimetres tall.

00:07:57.632 --> 00:08:00.844
Two stacked are eighty-six, and three are ninety-two.

00:08:01.527 --> 00:08:02.994
Each chair adds six.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.873
What happens when every step is the same?

00:08:09.195 --> 00:08:10.058
Here are the key notes.

00:08:10.461 --> 00:08:12.008
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:12.511
to copy them.
